Aboard a ship, everything now reads from ship time. The clock you are living by is the ship's, and the place you sailed from becomes an ordinary row with an offset like any other — on the map, in the list and on the widget.

A port's ring turns green when that port keeps your ship's clock, which is the moment you would otherwise work out whether to change your watch.

Routes and wakes start at the ship itself now, and widgets fit more in: full ship names, longer place names.
